<title>UK: Weather shuts Novorossiisk oil port,Tuapse reopens.</title>
<headline>Weather shuts Novorossiisk oil port,Tuapse reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk, Russia's main outlet for crude oil exports, was closed on Friday due to high winds and swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Odessa was also shut but the Tuapse terminal reopened after a three-day closure, the source added.</p>
<p>One crude tanker was alongside berth two at Novorossiisk but had not yet started to load.</p>
<p>Four more crude tankers were waiting at anchor outside the port, the source said.</p>
<p>The port of Ventspils on the Baltic was reported to be operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
